{"id": "z1132", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, a community. A community can refer to any large cluster of living things or elements that interact with each other in some way. An army of ants would be an example of a community because it consists of many individual ant s working together as a group. Similarly, a toy store and a shopping mall are examples of places where people gather for various purposes, but they do not necessarily involve a diverse range of living things like humans, dogs, and apple trees.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1140", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Feathers on s phinxes are primarily used for keeping warm. They provide insulation, helping the animal retain heat in cold environments. While some birds use feather s for flying or display ing, sphin xes lack feathers entirely, so their role is more about warmth and protection against the elements.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1148", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, ducks are water birds. So they like to live near water. The Sa hara is a desert with very little water. An tarctica has ice and snow but not much open water for ducks to swim in. The Appalachian Mountains have rivers and lakes where duck s can live. Death Valley is also very dry and hot, so it's not ideal for duck s. Therefore, the best choice would be C, the Appal achian Mountains.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1156", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When a circle is torn, it becomes a smaller circle. So the correct answer is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1164", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, water is essential for plant growth as it helps transport nutrient s and maintain cell structure. However, the best answer here would be option A, NH4, which stands for ammon ium. Ammonium nitrate is a common fertilizer that provides nitrogen, crucial for plant growth. While water is vital, it' s not the specific formula listed here that directly fuels plant development in this context.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1172", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's easier for humans to survive in a town. A cave can be dangerous due to low oxygen or unstable rock s, while the ocean is full of hazards like cold temperatures and predators. Being alone makes survival much harder without help. Towns offer shelter, food, water, medical care, and community support, making them the best option for human survival.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1180", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Deserts are characterized by high sunshine. So the answer is B, deserts get surplus sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1188", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most sound would come from D, the cha ssis of a car. Metal hitting metal is going to create the loudest noise.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1196", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, a plastic zip per. Mag nets are attracted to ferromagnetic materials like iron, ni ckel, and cobalt. Most plastic zippers contain metal components, often made of steel or another magnetic material, which allows them to be attracted to magnets. Flowing water does not have magnet ic properties that would attract a magnet. A car engine might have some magnetic parts, but it is not generally designed to be attractive to magnets in the same way as specific metal objects. A wooden desk contains no ferromagnetic materials, so it will not attract a magnet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1204", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The unit derived from the French word milliliter is typically used for volume measurement s in the range of A, one to 10 00 milliliters. So the correct answer is option A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1212", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A, the ice caps will completely melt if global warming continues. This is a hypothesis because it presents a specific prediction that can be tested through research and data collection.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1220", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, Athens. Athen s is known for its high humidity levels due to its Mediterranean climate, which often results in a lot of water vapor in the air.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
