{"id": "z1236", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "C. An octop us mimicking the color and texture of a rocky outcrop. This is a classic example of camouflage, where the octopus blend s into its surroundings to avoid detection by predator s or prey. While the other options involve behavior related to survival, only the octopus actively hide s through concealment.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1244", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If the population in a habitat is on a steady decline, it usually means that the environment is not supporting life well. So let's look at the options: A says it' s a place to emigrate from, which might be true but doesn't explain why people are leaving. B says it's an ideal habitat, but if people are leaving, it can't be ideal. C says it' s unsustainable, which fits because resources might be running out or conditions are getting worse. D says it's thriving, but declining population contradicts that. So the best answer is C: it is an unsustain able habitat.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1252", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Which of these situations is an example of pollutants? A. Plastic bags floating in the ocean, B. Mallard ducks floating on a lake, C. Cotton wood seeds floating in the air, D. Cirrus clouds floating in the sky?", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
