{"id": "z1932", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, if g of x is equal to f of negative x for all real numbers x, and 3, 2 is a point on the graph of g, then we can say that g of 3 equals 2. Now, since g of x is defined as f of negative x, substituting x with 3 gives us g of 3 equals f of negative 3. We already know g of 3 is 2, so this means f of negative 3 must be 2. Therefore, the point negative 3, 2 must be on the graph of f. Looking at the options, C, negative 3, 2, is the correct answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
